Look at this crazy cave, man!

2767
02:42:27,680 --> 02:42:28,420
It's so tall!

2768
02:42:32,150 --> 02:42:34,610
Wish I had night vision right now so I could see this properly.

2769
02:42:38,550 --> 02:42:40,110
Should be wary of these, uh...

2770
02:42:42,310 --> 02:42:42,930
Creepers here.

2771
02:42:44,970 --> 02:42:47,170
They could fall down on me and cause...

2772
02:42:47,810 --> 02:42:48,030
Problems.

2773
02:42:49,570 --> 02:42:53,310
And dying right here would actually be the most catastrophic thing that could ever happen to me.

2774
02:42:55,930 --> 02:42:58,010
So we really gotta keep an eye out.

2775
02:43:11,150 --> 02:43:13,110
Also, are we still running out of space here at all?

2776
02:43:14,410 --> 02:43:15,150
Not really.

2777
02:43:16,470 --> 02:43:17,530
Oh, it's digging fast.

2778
02:43:20,050 --> 02:43:20,870
We hit tough.

2779
02:43:22,050 --> 02:43:23,230
Tough is not that tough.

2780
02:43:23,390 --> 02:43:24,270
It's kind of a misnomer.

2781
02:43:33,460 --> 02:43:34,360
How much diamond?

2782
02:43:35,400 --> 02:43:35,840
20...

2783
02:43:35,840 --> 02:43:37,700
Okay, we're not finding that many more diamonds now.

2784
02:43:50,460 --> 02:43:50,900
Rail...

2785
02:43:50,900 --> 02:43:52,360
No, train...

2786
02:43:58,020 --> 02:43:58,460
Right.

2787
02:43:58,840 --> 02:44:01,360
We're actually getting everything we need to do the train today.

2788
02:44:13,070 --> 02:44:14,630
I really don't want to die here.

2789
02:44:22,750 --> 02:44:24,090
Do I have blast protection?

2790
02:44:26,610 --> 02:44:27,570
No, I don't.

2791
02:44:29,330 --> 02:44:31,470
Would love to have a lot of that against the creepers.

2792
02:44:33,370 --> 02:44:36,850
Because that is realistically the only thing that could really fuck up my day real fast.

2793
02:44:48,750 --> 02:44:49,450
Like this.

2794
02:44:49,610 --> 02:44:50,830
Openings in the ceiling scare me.

2795
02:45:03,110 --> 02:45:04,310
Close that shit off.

2796
02:45:08,780 --> 02:45:09,360
Open space.

2797
02:45:09,520 --> 02:45:10,100
Let's stay back a bit.

2798
02:45:15,540 --> 02:45:16,200
What's out there?

2799
02:45:19,530 --> 02:45:20,710
I think it's time to head home.

2800
02:45:25,680 --> 02:45:26,980
Oh, it's a...

2801
02:45:27,900 --> 02:45:28,220
Thingy.

2802
02:45:29,920 --> 02:45:30,520
Oh, lava!

2803
02:45:32,640 --> 02:45:32,960
Nope!

2804
02:45:33,520 --> 02:45:34,240
No, no, no.

2805
02:45:34,360 --> 02:45:35,300
Don't run off a cliff there.

2806
02:45:35,360 --> 02:45:36,460
I guess it could make a bridge.

2807
02:45:37,260 --> 02:45:39,500
Then we had lava over there as well, so that's kind of bad.

2808
02:45:42,020 --> 02:45:43,160
Oh, did I lose my arrow?

2809
02:45:43,340 --> 02:45:43,520
Shit.

2810
02:45:46,480 --> 02:45:47,580
I think it's time to leave.

2811
02:45:53,330 --> 02:45:54,270
Let's get out of here.

2812
02:45:55,390 --> 02:45:56,450
I'm gonna dig straight up.

2813
02:45:56,810 --> 02:45:57,710
Because I'm a real G.

2814
02:46:02,750 --> 02:46:03,290
See ya!

2815
02:46:06,430 --> 02:46:09,370
Guys, it's going to be day when I reach the surface.

2816
02:46:13,560 --> 02:46:14,920
And you can quote me on that.

2817
02:46:18,480 --> 02:46:20,120
Not gonna be a while until we do, though.

2818
02:46:36,670 --> 02:46:41,590
Guys, if it's day when I reach the surface, I'm going to stream tomorrow again.

2819
02:46:42,710 --> 02:46:45,350
If it's night, I'm not gonna stream for a whole week.

2820
02:47:01,760 --> 02:47:02,380
Get ready.

2821
02:47:14,740 --> 02:47:15,800
Don't even want to look around.

2822
02:47:15,960 --> 02:47:17,280
Actually, I do want to look a little bit.

2823
02:47:22,980 --> 02:47:24,160
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

2824
02:47:40,600 --> 02:47:41,780
It's been a while, huh?

2825
02:47:42,180 --> 02:47:43,380
Been a while since you did that to me.

2826
02:47:45,260 --> 02:47:45,620
Phew.

2827
02:47:47,380 --> 02:47:48,620
I almost forgot that was a thing.

2828
02:47:55,630 --> 02:47:56,490
Get ready for day.

2829
02:47:57,890 --> 02:47:58,490
Stream tomorrow.

2830
02:48:03,720 --> 02:48:04,080
Yikes.

2831
02:48:10,090 --> 02:48:11,170
You know what this means, right?

2832
02:48:11,910 --> 02:48:13,830
I'm probably gonna stream anyway.

2833
02:48:14,390 --> 02:48:18,650
Because I don't let random events dictate my existence.

2834
02:48:20,110 --> 02:48:20,990
That's right.

2835
02:48:23,840 --> 02:48:25,080
Fuck the bitrate.

2836
02:48:27,620 --> 02:48:28,480
What's that?

2837
02:48:29,360 --> 02:48:30,000
Is that lava?

2838
02:48:36,060 --> 02:48:37,140
Has to be, right?

2839
02:48:38,060 --> 02:48:38,740
Yeah, it's lava.

2840
02:48:43,570 --> 02:48:45,150
Wait, is that the same tower?

2841
02:48:47,880 --> 02:48:49,160
How am I here?

2842
02:48:50,240 --> 02:48:51,320
That's crazy.

2843
02:48:54,670 --> 02:48:55,170
Isn't it?

2844
02:48:57,970 --> 02:48:59,790
I do want to try and find another igloo.

2845
02:49:01,590 --> 02:49:02,310
Let's go to bed.

2846
02:49:07,200 --> 02:49:09,360
You can't find an igloo on an empty stomach, right?

2847
02:49:09,420 --> 02:49:10,300
So we go to sleep first.

2848
02:49:28,220 --> 02:49:28,900
Okay, guys.

2849
02:49:29,060 --> 02:49:31,100
I need you all to be on the lookout for an igloo.

2850
02:49:38,480 --> 02:49:42,300
And if you do see one, really make it clear in chat, okay?

2851
02:49:45,700 --> 02:49:46,620
Wait, we got one!

2852
02:49:46,740 --> 02:49:47,700
Unless that's the same one.

2853
02:49:50,830 --> 02:49:51,570
There's no way.

2854
02:49:53,690 --> 02:49:54,130
Oh!

2855
02:49:56,890 --> 02:49:57,670
God dang.

2856
02:50:06,060 --> 02:50:07,800
I'm gonna find another igloo.

2857
02:50:13,430 --> 02:50:14,830
There's sand here for some reason.

2858
02:50:14,970 --> 02:50:15,730
That's kind of odd.

2859
02:50:18,110 --> 02:50:19,230
Oh, those are pumpkins.

2860
02:50:20,710 --> 02:50:21,630
Speaking of pumpkins.

2861
02:50:22,750 --> 02:50:26,970
I was considering buying one the other day and then carving it for Halloween.

2862
02:50:29,510 --> 02:50:30,430
Maybe we should do it.

2863
02:50:36,070 --> 02:50:36,350
Oh!

2864
02:50:36,510 --> 02:50:36,710
Oh!

2865
02:50:37,310 --> 02:50:37,330
Oh!

2866
02:50:37,330 --> 02:50:37,390
Oh!

2867
02:50:37,630 --> 02:50:37,770
Oh!

2868
02:50:37,770 --> 02:50:38,450
Would you look at that?

2869
02:50:41,600 --> 02:50:42,540
I'll take some obsidian.

2870
02:50:47,580 --> 02:50:48,520
Because check it out!

2871
02:50:49,640 --> 02:50:50,880
I am just gonna...

2872
02:50:50,880 --> 02:50:51,740
Wait, where are my tracks?

2873
02:50:54,060 --> 02:50:56,600
Oh, I can't pull this out unless we have tracks!

2874
02:51:05,350 --> 02:51:06,770
Well, that's a bummer.

2875
02:51:31,620 --> 02:51:33,940
Guys, I predict inside here...

2876
02:51:34,580 --> 02:51:35,600
there's going to be...

2877
02:51:36,420 --> 02:51:37,200
a fortress.

2878
02:51:49,140 --> 02:51:50,860
Wait, can I even light this thing?

2879
02:51:52,500 --> 02:51:53,320
Yes, I can.

2880
02:52:01,630 --> 02:52:04,310
Why am I always forgetting the frickin' shape of this?

2881
02:52:05,610 --> 02:52:06,590
Like there, right?

2882
02:52:31,960 --> 02:52:32,960
No fortress?

2883
02:52:35,700 --> 02:52:37,220
No, no, no, it's here, it's here.

2884
02:52:40,220 --> 02:52:41,280
I'm never wrong.

2885
02:52:41,540 --> 02:52:42,500
Wait, I'm wrong?

2886
02:52:43,500 --> 02:52:44,680
I'm not used to this.

2887
02:52:47,850 --> 02:52:48,830
But... but...

2888
02:52:48,830 --> 02:52:49,690
I'm always right.

2889
02:52:55,080 --> 02:52:56,600
Huh, so that's how that feels.

2890
02:52:58,860 --> 02:52:59,660
Being wrong.

2891
02:53:19,820 --> 02:53:21,520
Had to have him sooner or later, right?

2892
02:53:29,630 --> 02:53:30,590
Let's go back in.

2893
02:53:41,760 --> 02:53:43,280
I guess we just keep flying.

2894
02:53:44,740 --> 02:53:45,840
How's my durability?

2895
02:53:46,100 --> 02:53:47,100
It's great, we're chilling.

2896
02:53:48,520 --> 02:53:49,260
Uh, igloo hunting.

2897
02:53:52,230 --> 02:53:53,830
Let's really look now.

2898
02:53:55,630 --> 02:53:56,570
Are you looking?

2899
02:54:06,320 --> 02:54:07,480
I hate...

2900
02:54:07,890 --> 02:54:09,140
the possibility...

2901
02:54:09,140 --> 02:54:11,720
of the igloo being inside like a forest.

2902
02:54:12,480 --> 02:54:15,020
Because if it is, I will have no chance to see it.

2903
02:54:15,460 --> 02:54:16,220
From the air.

2904
02:54:17,140 --> 02:54:18,280
Maybe I'll walk through it a bit.

2905
02:54:23,470 --> 02:54:24,390
We'll see how it goes.

2906
02:54:33,110 --> 02:54:34,190
Wait, are these ferns?

2907
02:54:34,470 --> 02:54:35,750
Oh, I guess I can't check.

2908
02:54:36,790 --> 02:54:37,910
No, these are ferns.

2909
02:54:37,990 --> 02:54:38,450
These are ferns.

2910
02:54:57,800 --> 02:54:58,740
A little village.

2911
02:55:09,120 --> 02:55:10,980
This can never be an igloo, I don't think.

2912
02:55:11,920 --> 02:55:14,400
Yeah, they look like igloos, but they're fake.

2913
02:55:20,480 --> 02:55:22,160
Now, what are these guys eating though?

2914
02:55:28,310 --> 02:55:29,730
Oh wait, we should get cats.

2915
02:55:29,950 --> 02:55:31,210
I don't even have any cats.

2916
02:55:35,060 --> 02:55:36,280
But we need fish for that.

2917
02:55:39,900 --> 02:55:41,580
Yo, what are y'all eating in this village?

2918
02:55:43,880 --> 02:55:45,060
I guess fish, maybe?

2919
02:55:47,950 --> 02:55:49,390
Maybe that's why you also have cats?

2920
02:55:53,040 --> 02:55:53,740
Brother, what?

2921
02:55:54,180 --> 02:55:54,960
No chests?

2922
02:55:55,440 --> 02:55:56,100
What are you?

2923
02:55:58,000 --> 02:55:59,220
Some kind of hunter or something?

2924
02:56:00,960 --> 02:56:02,460
How come I can't...

2925
02:56:02,460 --> 02:56:04,280
Oh, maybe that's just your standard look.

2926
02:56:09,810 --> 02:56:10,790
We keep moving.

2927
02:56:12,890 --> 02:56:14,150
Keep looking for igloo.

2928
02:56:18,740 --> 02:56:19,940
I'm looking at chat!

2929
02:56:23,550 --> 02:56:24,610
I stopped looking.

2930
02:56:30,340 --> 02:56:32,820
I'm gonna look again in 10 seconds.

2931
02:56:47,420 --> 02:56:49,960
Wait, where's the goddamn igloo?

2932
02:56:50,180 --> 02:56:52,140
Show me the igloo, damn it.

2933
02:56:55,320 --> 02:56:57,460
Oh, that's so stupid.

2934
02:56:58,320 --> 02:56:59,960
Hey, that's so picturesque!

2935
02:57:01,940 --> 02:57:03,920
Look at that little green island there!

2936
02:57:07,440 --> 02:57:07,920
Yo!

2937
02:57:09,260 --> 02:57:10,760
I kinda wanna have a little hut.

2938
02:57:13,220 --> 02:57:14,620
Also, we're running low on rockets.

2939
02:57:14,680 --> 02:57:15,860
Maybe it's time to start hitting home.

2940
02:57:18,870 --> 02:57:19,550
That way.

2941
02:57:23,100 --> 02:57:24,480
That's so nice looking, man.

2942
02:57:27,000 --> 02:57:27,800
Very pretty.

2943
02:57:27,920 --> 02:57:28,200
What's that?

2944
02:57:29,200 --> 02:57:29,920
It's ice.

2945
02:57:30,840 --> 02:57:31,760
Ice baby.

2946
02:57:31,760 --> 02:57:31,880
Maybe.

2947
02:57:32,640 --> 02:57:33,620
Do-do-do-do-do-do-do.

2948
02:57:36,320 --> 02:57:36,840
Ah...

2949
02:57:37,380 --> 02:57:39,260
Let's start going home.

2950
02:57:39,940 --> 02:57:41,660
And then we look for igloo on the way.

2951
02:57:50,820 --> 02:57:52,800
Wait, am I really back at that same tower?

2952
02:57:52,920 --> 02:57:53,880
I'm going in circles.

2953
02:57:55,160 --> 02:57:56,180
How is this possible?

2954
02:58:12,790 --> 02:58:13,870
What is that?

2955
02:58:15,810 --> 02:58:16,670
Hold the phone.

2956
02:58:21,360 --> 02:58:22,980
I've seen something like that before.

2957
02:58:40,470 --> 02:58:41,350
Abandoned village.

2958
02:59:01,190 --> 02:59:01,750
Cats?

2959
02:59:02,830 --> 02:59:03,390
Where?

2960
02:59:10,160 --> 02:59:11,240
You're down there.

2961
02:59:16,720 --> 02:59:17,780
What's going on?

2962
02:59:21,950 --> 02:59:23,170
Village is reopened.

2963
02:59:26,660 --> 02:59:27,940
Someone left in a hurry.

2964
02:59:28,260 --> 02:59:29,020
What's behind their bread?

2965
02:59:32,250 --> 02:59:33,350
I mean...

2966
02:59:33,350 --> 02:59:34,110
Come on, guys.

2967
02:59:34,450 --> 02:59:37,370
They have two basins of water here, right next to that bread basket.

2968
02:59:42,100 --> 02:59:42,320
Oh.

2969
02:59:43,120 --> 02:59:44,220
Oi, oi, oi, oi, oi.

2970
02:59:45,320 --> 02:59:47,420
This is an infected villager.

2971
02:59:49,100 --> 02:59:50,760
Unfortunately, I can't do anything about that.

2972
02:59:51,080 --> 02:59:52,900
I don't have the necessary requirements.

2973
02:59:54,220 --> 02:59:55,560
I see money.

2974
02:59:58,270 --> 02:59:59,510
Oh, nice.

2975
03:00:01,710 --> 03:00:03,570
So what the hell is this place even?

2976
03:00:05,410 --> 03:00:07,030
Why am I so intrigued by it?

2977
03:00:07,570 --> 03:00:08,690
Oh, let's actually go to bed.

2978
03:00:16,160 --> 03:00:16,640
Ah!

2979
03:00:16,920 --> 03:00:17,440
Oh, God.

2980
03:00:19,460 --> 03:00:20,040
How the...

2981
03:00:22,290 --> 03:00:23,570
How the hell do I get out of this?

2982
03:00:25,730 --> 03:00:26,090
Hello?

2983
03:00:34,000 --> 03:00:34,880
Are you kidding me?

2984
03:00:35,200 --> 03:00:35,560
Oh, okay.

2985
03:00:35,660 --> 03:00:36,040
Okay, here we go.

2986
03:00:36,100 --> 03:00:36,300
Here we go.

2987
03:00:37,520 --> 03:00:37,880
Jesus.

2988
03:00:41,560 --> 03:00:42,980
It's like impossible to get out of.

2989
03:00:48,860 --> 03:00:50,080
What a weird place.

2990
03:00:52,560 --> 03:00:54,200
Oh, that's so green looking.

2991
03:00:55,080 --> 03:00:56,540
After you've seen all this white, you know?

2992
03:01:12,620 --> 03:01:14,120
There's still a chance we find an igloo.

2993
03:01:16,600 --> 03:01:17,920
We keep our eyes peeled.

2994
03:01:27,790 --> 03:01:28,650
I have to.

2995
03:01:28,870 --> 03:01:30,010
I can't not do it.

2996
03:01:31,710 --> 03:01:32,750
Also, I will take this.

2997
03:01:36,560 --> 03:01:38,100
Wait, it works next to ice?

2998
03:01:40,540 --> 03:01:41,020
Interesting.

2999
03:01:47,430 --> 03:01:48,150
Silk touch.

3000
03:02:01,820 --> 03:02:02,500
Ah, wait.

3001
03:02:02,500 --> 03:02:03,920
I don't have enough obsidian for this.

3002
03:02:10,730 --> 03:02:11,990
I can't even light it.

3003
03:02:12,590 --> 03:02:13,210
Yeah, okay.

3004
03:02:13,330 --> 03:02:13,490
Whatever.

3005
03:02:14,730 --> 03:02:15,190
Never mind.

3006
03:02:22,200 --> 03:02:23,320
Okay, igloo time.

3007
03:02:23,740 --> 03:02:24,240
Come on.

3008
03:02:24,540 --> 03:02:25,400
Show yourself.

3009
03:02:25,400 --> 03:02:28,140
I really need this recipe.

3010
03:02:47,050 --> 03:02:47,470
What?

3011
03:02:47,730 --> 03:02:47,850
Oh.

3012
03:02:48,310 --> 03:02:49,030
Rabbits.

3013
03:02:56,950 --> 03:02:58,930
It should be easy to see something here.

3014
03:03:05,570 --> 03:03:06,510
But no.

3015
03:03:07,550 --> 03:03:08,530
Ten rockets left.

3016
03:03:17,780 --> 03:03:19,080
A little village.

3017
03:03:26,540 --> 03:03:27,780
Show me the glue.

3018
03:03:30,200 --> 03:03:32,040
They are so incredibly rare.

3019
03:03:37,000 --> 03:03:37,520
What's that?

3020
03:03:38,760 --> 03:03:39,520
It's a weird tree.

3021
03:03:46,330 --> 03:03:47,070
Hey, you know what?

3022
03:03:47,170 --> 03:03:48,050
Maybe these guys have carrots.

3023
03:03:48,550 --> 03:03:49,410
I kind of need that.

3024
03:03:49,690 --> 03:03:51,190
Would be nice to get that on the way home, too.

3025
03:03:53,490 --> 03:03:54,810
Looks like a carrot village to me.

3026
03:03:56,150 --> 03:03:58,330
It's hard to explain why, but it just does, you know?

3027
03:04:02,630 --> 03:04:03,590
Damn, that's expensive.

3028
03:04:04,390 --> 03:04:05,250
Think I'm made of money?

3029
03:04:17,710 --> 03:04:18,690
Looks like bread people.

3030
03:04:20,970 --> 03:04:21,830
No carrots here.

3031
03:04:21,930 --> 03:04:22,830
What are you doing on the roof?

3032
03:04:24,390 --> 03:04:25,110
You're unemployed.

3033
03:04:31,340 --> 03:04:31,980
Pumpkin pie.

3034
03:04:31,980 --> 03:04:32,600
I'll eat that.

3035
03:04:48,640 --> 03:04:49,560
Could have been special.

3036
03:04:50,920 --> 03:04:51,720
But it wasn't.

3037
03:04:55,030 --> 03:04:55,770
Alright, let's leave.

3038
03:05:00,640 --> 03:05:01,140
Oh, wait.

3039
03:05:01,200 --> 03:05:01,840
Are we close to home?

3040
03:05:01,880 --> 03:05:03,580
This may be the village right next to my home.

3041
03:05:04,140 --> 03:05:05,120
I recognize this.

